<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details" id="dev-penalties">
    <summary>Late penalties, posting and Friction Feedback</summary>
    <div>
        <ul>
            <li><code>penalty\compat::unified()</code> is true once <code>mod_quiz</code> has core due dates (Moodle 5.3). One release serves 5.1, 5.2 and 5.3.</li>
            <li><code>penalty\service::resync()</code> recalculates a student's penalties. Observers call it on <code>user_graded</code>, quiz attempt submission, assignment extensions, and assignment and quiz overrides.</li>
            <li><code>penalty\gradebook_writer</code> writes the total deduction to <code>grade_grades.deductedmark</code>; the raw grade is untouched and nothing is overridden.</li>
            <li>The per-activity switch is in <code>local_unifiedgrader_penset</code> and travels with backup and restore.</li>
            <li>Posting the class is the grade item's hidden flag; posting a student or a group is <code>grade_grades.hidden</code> on their cell (<code>classes/grades/</code>).</li>
            <li>A Friction Feedback walk is a row in <code>local_unifiedgrader_friction</code> that holds the cell hidden until the student finishes or <code>task\open_friction</code> opens it.</li>
            <li><code>dates\student_dates</code> loads, previews and saves the Dates &amp; extensions dialogue through the activities' own APIs.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details" id="dev-annotations">
    <summary>Annotations: from marks on screen to a PDF</summary>
    <div>
        <p>Documents are drawn with PDF.js. Marks are drawn on a Fabric.js layer over each page and
        saved per page as JSON in <code>local_unifiedgrader_annot</code>. On save, pdf-lib draws the
        marks into a real PDF, stored in the <code>annotatedpdf</code> file area for the student to
        download. All three libraries ship in <code>thirdparty/</code>; nothing is loaded from elsewhere.</p>
