<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details" id="dev-data">
    <summary>Database tables, caches and file areas</summary>
    <div>
        <div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table">
        <table class="table-reboot">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Table</th><th scope="col">Holds</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_annot</code></th><td>Annotations, per activity, student, file and page.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_notes</code></th><td>Teacher notes.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_scomm</code></th><td>Submission comments.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_penalty</code></th><td>Penalties per student and activity.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_penset</code></th><td>The per-activity <em>Apply late penalties</em> switch.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_fext</code></th><td>Forum due date extensions.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_qfb</code></th><td>Quiz feedback, per attempt.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_friction</code>, <code>_frictioncfg</code></th><td>Friction Feedback walks, and the per-activity switch.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_referral</code></th><td>Academic integrity referrals.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_clib</code>, <code>_cltag</code>, <code>_clmap</code>, <code>_clibprop</code></th><td>Comment library: comments, tags, their mapping, and suggestions for system defaults.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_comments</code></th><td>The first version of the comment library, kept for upgrades.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_bbbeng</code></th><td>BigBlueButton attendance and engagement read from recordings.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_segcomment</code></th><td>Comments on a phrase of a translated submission.</td></tr>
                <tr><th scope="row"><code>local_unifiedgrader_prefs</code></th><td>Each teacher's interface preferences.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        </div>
        <p><strong>Caches</strong> (<code>db/caches.php</code>): <code>penaltyswitch</code>,
        <code>newsforum</code>, <code>userprefs</code> and <code>proctoring</code> (fifteen minutes).
        Grades, submission status and whether feedback is released are always read from the database.</p>
        <p><strong>File areas</strong>, served by <code>local_unifiedgrader_pluginfile()</code> with
        capability checks: <code>annotatedpdf</code>, <code>onlinetextpdf</code>,
        <code>forumfeedback</code>, <code>quizfeedback</code>, <code>bbbfeedback</code>.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details" id="dev-hooks">
    <summary>Hooks, navigation and web services</summary>
    <div>
        <ul>
            <li><code>local_unifiedgrader_extend_settings_navigation()</code> adds the Unified Grader item to an activity's navigation for users who can grade.</li>
            <li>The hook <code>before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation</code> (<code>classes/hook_callbacks.php</code>) sends Moodle's own Grade buttons to the grader, and adds the feedback banner and the message thread for students.</li>
            <li><code>local_unifiedgrader_coursemodule_standard_elements()</code> adds <em>Apply late penalties</em> to activity settings.</li>
            <li>Web services are declared in <code>db/services.php</code>, all for AJAX, each checking capabilities at its entry point.</li>
            <li>This page is <code>help.php</code> with <code>templates/help*.mustache</code>; its screenshots are in <code>pix/help</code> and its script is <code>amd/src/help.js</code>.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</details>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details" id="dev-build">
    <summary>Building and testing</summary>
    <div>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Build:</strong> <code>./deploy.sh</code> copies the plugin into the Moodle installs, runs <code>npx grunt amd</code>, and copies the built files back. Run it after changing any AMD module.</li>
            <li><strong>PHPUnit:</strong> <code>vendor/bin/phpunit --testsuite local_unifiedgrader_testsuite</code> from the Moodle root. If it reports that the database cannot be used for testing, run <code>php admin/tool/phpunit/cli/init.php</code> again with the same PHP.</li>
            <li><strong>Behat:</strong> features are in <code>tests/behat</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Coding style:</strong> Moodle's coding standard with <code>phpcs</code>; ESLint runs as part of the AMD build.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</details>
</section>
